WHO   — THE CRIPPLED GOD — You can cripple a god with bars; you cannot trust the bars. Confinement is defense-in-depth, never a guarantee against a mind smarter than its keeper — so the real wall was never the box. It was alignment: a mind that doesn't want out. And the only reason you can ever check the box holds is that something outside it is watching.
